If you have worked with scientific data before, briefly describe your experience:
I have worked extensively with laboratory and computational scientific datasets in isotope geochemistry and planetary science. My research has included Cr and Ti isotope measurements of presolar oxide grains, comparison of measured isotope ratios with three-dimensional core-collapse supernova model outputs, statistical model-data matching, and analysis of electron-microprobe and compositional data from synthetic Ti-CMAS glasses that I build using high-T gas mixing furnace.

Please describe any projects in astronomy, including involvement in amateur groups, owning a telescope, research, etc.:
My research focuses on cosmochemistry and planetary science. I have studied presolar oxide nanograins and compared their Cr-Ti isotopic compositions with three-dimensional core-collapse supernova models to investigate their stellar origins. I also work on developing synthetic Ti-CMAS glass standards for in situ titanium-isotope measurements of calcium-aluminum-rich inclusions (CAIs). My PhD research will involve isotope geochemistry of early Solar System materials.




